class:: ERBBands
summary:: ERB spaced triangular spectral bands
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/MFCC2

description::
Glasberg and Moore (1990) ERB-rate mapping: E(f) = 21.4 * log10(1 + 0.00437 * f), with f in Hz. Source: link::https://doi.org/10.1016/0378-5955(90)90170-T::.

The bank places numBands+2 equally spaced points on that named scale, converts them to Hz, and builds piecewise-linear triangular filters in Hz. Each output is sum(weight * spectrum). Normalized mode divides each filter by the sum of its sampled FFT-bin weights. Filters with no sampled support return zero; increase fftSize or reduce numBands if low-frequency filters are narrower than the FFT resolution. Power mode squares the raw FFT magnitude before filtering. Silence returns zero.

All configuration except chain is read at construction. The weight matrix occupies 8 * numBands * (fftSize/2+1) bytes and processing is O(numBands * fftSize) per frame, with no runtime allocation or extra lookahead. A 1024-sample FFT window is 21.3 ms at 48 kHz.

Vanilla link::Classes/MFCC:: combines Mel bands and a cepstral transform; ERBBands exposes its ERB bands directly for musical control, without a DCT.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
FFT chain with a buffer matching fftSize.
argument:: numBands
Literal integer 4..128. Output count.
argument:: minFreq
Lower filterbank edge in Hz. Default 20.
argument:: maxFreq
Upper filterbank edge in Hz. Zero selects Nyquist.
argument:: normalize
Positive gives a discrete weighted mean per band; 0 gives a weighted sum.
argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 magnitude or 1 power. Default 1.
argument:: fftSize
Literal power of two 256..8192, matching the FFT buffer.
returns::
One control per band in ascending center-frequency order.

examples::
The band-energy distribution controls an eight-sine resynthesis. Listen to the quiet original beside a moving harmonic color driven by the analysis.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot {
    Routine({
        var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
        s.sync;
        ~mir2Example = {
            var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1);
            // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
            var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
            var bands = ERBBands.kr(chain, numBands: 8, minFreq: 100, maxFreq: 6000, fftSize: 1024);
            var balance = bands / (bands.sum + 1e-9);
            var level = Amplitude.kr(source, 0.01, 0.1);
            var voice = Mix(SinOsc.ar([180, 240, 320, 430, 580, 780, 1050, 1400], 0, Lag.kr(balance, 0.04))) * level;
            var fade = Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2);
            ((source * 0.06) + (voice * 0.2)) * fade ! 2
        }.play;
        ~mir2Example.onFree { buffer.free };
    }).play(AppClock);
};
)

// Stop and free the sample buffer.
(
~mir2Example.free;
)
::

